INT. LIBRARY OF MOTHS - THE HOLLOW TOWER - NIGHT

Shelves rise into darkness, thick with bound ledgers. Pale moths cover every spine, their wings turning the pages by themselves.

ORRIN, a young knight in dented mail, steps through the arch, sword half-drawn. At his side, SABLE, a thief with a hooded cloak and a crooked smile, carries a lantern whose flame burns blue.

ORRIN
Quiet. They sleep.

SABLE
They're moths, Orrin. They don't sleep.

TAMSIN, a girl of twelve in an apprentice's smock, scurries from behind a shelf, arms full of scrolls, and nearly collides with them. All three freeze.

TAMSIN
You are not supposed to be here.

SABLE
No one is.

The moths lift in a silent cloud. Orrin's sword rings free. Sable ducks, Tamsin shrieks, scrolls scatter, and the three tumble together into the center aisle, tangled in cloak and chain.

A hush falls.

VESPER, tall and thin, robed in gray, steps from between the shelves. Her face is a smooth mask of bone-white silk. She raises one hand. The moths settle.

VESPER
The Archivist welcomes you. Now put down the lantern.
